# TypeScript Strictness

## Rules

- Always use strict TypeScript
- Never use `any`, unsafe casting, or loosely typed objects
- Prefer explicit interfaces and reusable types from `src/types/`

## Bad vs Good

```ts
// BAD
const data: any = response;

// GOOD
interface WeddingData {
  brideName: string;
  groomName: string;
}
```

## Shared Schema

- `WeddingData` and related types live in `src/types/` — import, don't redefine per feature
- Template props must use shared types, not ad-hoc shapes

## Server vs Client

- Type server action inputs/outputs explicitly
- Use `Database` types from Supabase generated types when available
